.TH APPSCAN 1 "September 2026" "appscan 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
appscan \- scan documents and photos with SANE scanners
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B appscan
.RB [ gui
.RB [ \-d
.IR NAME ]]
.br
.B appscan scan
.I OUTPUT
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B appscan list
.br
.B appscan warmup
.RB [ \-d
.IR NAME ]
.br
.B appscan reset
.br
.B appscan firmware
.br
.B appscan setup
.RB [ \-\-remove ]
.br
.B appscan
.BR \-\-version " | " \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B appscan
is a command\-line tool and GTK graphical interface for scanners supported by
SANE.
Every scan is performed by
.BR scanimage (1),
and the choices offered for each option (modes, resolutions, sources and so
on) are read from the selected scanner with
.BR "scanimage \-A" .
Nothing has to run as root and no changes to
.I /etc/sane.d
are needed.
.PP
Most scanners work without any special handling.
Models that need more get a built\-in
.IR "quirk profile" ,
matched by SANE backend and USB ID.
A profile gives the scanner a private SANE configuration, the firmware it
needs, a lamp warm\-up, and a safe way to cancel: if interrupting the scanner
before image data flows would leave it hanging,
.B appscan
kills
.BR scanimage (1)
and resets the scanner over USB instead.
The only profile so far is for the Epson Perfection 2480 PHOTO and 2580 PHOTO
.RB ( snapscan
backend, USB ID 04b8:0121).
.PP
The Epson scanners need Epson's firmware uploaded every time they are powered
on.
Run
.B appscan firmware
once to download and install it; after that, the upload happens automatically
the first time the scanner is used after power\-on.
The Epson scanners cannot be used until the firmware is installed.
.SS "Graphical interface"
Without a command,
.B appscan
opens a GTK4/libadwaita window.
Starting it again brings the open window to the front.
.PP
The sidebar has three groups.
.B Scanner
selects the device, with a button to look for scanners again.
.B Settings
has drop\-down lists for source, mode, resolution and depth, and sliders for
brightness and contrast; a setting the scanner does not have is hidden, and
one the current mode does not use (brightness, contrast and depth in
.B Lineart
mode on the Epson) is disabled.
The sliders cover the scanner's range, limited to \-100 to 100, in steps of 5;
double\-click a slider to reset it.
.B Multi\-page PDF
shows the number of pages waiting to be saved and has the
.BR "Add page" ,
.B "Save PDF\&...\&"
and
.B Discard
buttons.
Every page keeps the settings it was scanned with, so the resolution and mode
can change between pages.
.PP
The header bar has
.B Preview
(a quick low\-resolution scan of the whole area),
.B Scan\&...\&
(asks where to save the file; as with
.BR "appscan scan" ,
its extension selects the format), and
.B Cancel
while a task is running.
Drag on the preview to select the area to scan; without a selection the whole
area is scanned.
Changing the source clears the preview and the selection.
A progress bar and a status line follow the running task, and short
notifications report saved files, added pages and cancelled scans.
.PP
On start the GUI looks for scanners and reads the options of the selected
one; for a scanner whose profile needs a warm\-up it also warms up the lamp,
and the scan buttons stay disabled until that is done.
Closing the window, or pressing
.B Ctrl\-C
in the terminal that started it, cancels a running scan (or waits for a file
being written), and asks first if PDF pages have not been saved.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBgui\fR [\fB\-d\fR \fINAME\fR]
Open the graphical interface.
This is the default when no command is given.
.TP
.BI scan " OUTPUT"
Scan to the file
.IR OUTPUT .
The file type is chosen by its extension; see
.B "Options for scan"
below.
Progress is printed on standard error.
.B Ctrl\-C
cancels the scan.
For a scanner with a profile such as the Epson, a cancel before image data
starts flowing, or one that does not finish within 10 seconds, kills
.BR scanimage (1)
and resets the scanner, whose lamp must then warm up again.
.TP
.B list
List the detected scanners, one per line: the SANE device name, a tab, and a
description.
Scanners with a quirk profile come first, followed by all the other SANE
devices.
Device names such as
.B snapscan:libusb:001:011
contain USB bus and device numbers, which change whenever the scanner is
replugged.
.TP
\fBwarmup\fR [\fB\-d\fR \fINAME\fR]
Switch the lamp on and wait until it is warm, so that the next scan starts
immediately.
The lamp of the Epson scanners needs about 30\(en40 seconds after power\-on or
a reset.
.TP
.B reset
Reset the USB connection of every connected scanner that has a quirk profile,
which has the same effect as unplugging and replugging it.
Use it when such a scanner stops responding.
The lamp needs to warm up again afterwards.
.TP
.B firmware
Install the firmware for the profiles that need one.
For the Epson 2480/2580 this downloads Epson's Windows driver (Epson Scan
3.04A) from
.br
\%https://ftp.epson.com/drivers/epson12204.exe,
.br
extracts
.I esfw41.bin
from it, verifies its SHA\-256 checksum and installs it.
The same file serves both the 2480 and the 2580.
The firmware is proprietary software of Seiko Epson Corporation;
.B appscan
does not include or redistribute it.
.TP
\fBsetup\fR [\fB\-\-remove\fR]
Install the desktop menu entry (pointing at the absolute path of the running
binary), the application icon and this manual page under
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME ,
then refresh the icon cache and the manual page index when possible.
It also removes the desktop entry of older versions.
With
.BR \-\-remove ,
delete those files and the data directory
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/appscan
(firmware and SANE configuration) instead; the binary itself is left in place.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Global options"
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
Also accepted after a command, as in
.BR "appscan scan \-h" .
.SS "Options for gui, scan and warmup"
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-device\fR \fINAME\fR
The SANE device to use, as printed by
.BR "appscan list" .
Default: the first scanner in that list.
.SS "Options for scan"
The valid values of
.BR \-\-mode ,
.BR \-\-resolution ,
.BR \-\-depth ,
.BR \-\-source ,
.BR \-\-area ,
.B \-\-brightness
and
.B \-\-contrast
depend on the scanner, and the values in this section are those of the Epson
Perfection 2480 PHOTO.
Run
.B scanimage \-d
.I NAME
.B \-A
to see what another scanner offers.
A value that is not one of the scanner's choices or is out of its range, or an
option the scanner does not have, is a usage error.
An option that is inactive in the chosen mode or source is silently ignored.
When an option is not given, the scanner's default is used.
.TP
.I OUTPUT
The file to write.
Its extension selects the format:
.BR .png ,
.B .jpg
or
.BR .jpeg ,
.B .tif
or
.BR .tiff ,
.BR .pnm ,
.BR .pdf ,
in upper or lower case.
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fIMODE\fR
Colour mode; on the Epson one of
.BR Color ,
.BR Halftone ,
.B Gray
or
.BR Lineart .
.B Lineart
produces pure black and white, suited to text and fax\-like documents; the
Epson ignores
.BR \-\-brightness ,
.B \-\-contrast
and
.B \-\-depth
in this mode.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-resolution\fR \fIDPI\fR
Resolution in dots per inch; on the Epson one of 50, 75, 100, 150, 200, 300,
400, 600, 1200 or 2400, with 300 as the default.
.TP
\fB\-\-depth\fR \fIN\fR
Bits per colour channel; 8 or 16 on the Epson.
A depth of 16 needs
.BR .png ,
.B .tif
(or
.BR .tiff )
or
.B .pnm
output; with
.B .jpg
or
.B .jpeg
it is an error.
The depth is ignored for
.B .pdf
output.
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fISOURCE\fR
Where to scan from; on the Epson
.B Flatbed
or
.BR "\(dqTransparency Adapter\(dq" ,
the unit for film and slides, whose scan area is 55\(mu125\ mm on the 2480
(see
.B BUGS
for the 2580).
Quote a value that contains a space.
.TP
\fB\-\-area\fR \fILEFT TOP WIDTH HEIGHT\fR
The area to scan, in millimetres, measured from the top\-left corner of the
scan area of the source.
Decimal values are accepted.
Default: the whole scan area of the source (216\(mu297\ mm on the flatbed of
the Epson).
.TP
\fB\-\-brightness\fR \fIPERCENT\fR
Brightness adjustment, a whole number; from \-400 to 400 on the Epson.
.TP
\fB\-\-contrast\fR \fIPERCENT\fR
Contrast adjustment, a whole number; from \-100 to 400 on the Epson.
.TP
\fB\-\-pages\fR \fIN\fR
Only for PDF output: scan
.I N
pages into one PDF file.
A value other than 1 with an output that is not
.BR .pdf ,
or a value below 1, is a usage error.
Before each page after the first,
.B appscan
waits for Enter on standard input, giving you time to place the next sheet.
Stopping early, with
.B Ctrl\-C
or end of input (\fBCtrl\-D\fR), still saves the pages scanned so far;
if no page has been scanned yet, nothing is saved and the scan counts as
cancelled.
If a page fails, the pages scanned before it are saved too, and the error is
reported afterwards.
Default: 1.
.PP
The folder of
.I OUTPUT
must be writable; this is checked before scanning starts.
.PP
.B appscan
assembles PDF files itself and encodes each page on its own: colour and grey
pages are 8 bits per channel and JPEG\-compressed, and
.B Lineart
pages are 1 bit per pixel and lossless, even in a PDF that mixes both kinds
(possible in the GUI).
Each page size matches the scanned area at the resolution of that page.
An existing file is replaced only once the new PDF has been written
completely.
.SH EXAMPLES
List the connected scanners (the two fields are separated by a tab):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ appscan list
snapscan:libusb:001:011	Epson Perfection 2480/2580 PHOTO
.EE
.RE
.PP
Quick colour scan of a document with the scanner's default settings:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan letter.png
.EE
.RE
.PP
Greyscale scan at 600\ dpi with a specific scanner:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan \-d snapscan:libusb:001:011 \-\-mode Gray \-r 600 page.png
.EE
.RE
.PP
Crop a 15\(mu10\ cm photo lying 20\ mm from the left edge and 30\ mm from the
top of the glass, saved as a JPEG:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan \-r 600 \-\-area 20 30 150 100 holiday.jpg
.EE
.RE
.PP
Archival scan of a photo as a 16\-bit TIFF:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan \-r 1200 \-\-depth 16 \-\-area 0 0 130 180 grandma.tif
.EE
.RE
.PP
Film or slides through the transparency adapter of a 2480 at 2400\ dpi
(the whole 55\(mu125\ mm area in 16\-bit colour is about 370\ MB):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan \-\-source "Transparency Adapter" \-r 2400 \e
    \-\-depth 16 \-\-area 0 0 55 125 film\-01.tif
.EE
.RE
.PP
A four\-page contract in one PDF; press Enter after placing each new sheet:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan \-\-mode Gray \-r 200 \-\-pages 4 contract.pdf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Brighten a faded page and raise its contrast:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan \-\-brightness 30 \-\-contrast 40 faded.png
.EE
.RE
.PP
Lineart at 300\ dpi for plain text or fax\-like documents:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan \-\-mode Lineart \-r 300 memo.png
.EE
.RE
.PP
Warm the lamp up first in a script, so the scans start without delay:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
#!/bin/sh
set \-e
appscan warmup
appscan scan \-r 600 cover.png
appscan scan \-r 600 back.png
.EE
.RE
.PP
Batch loop naming each file by date and time; type
.B q
at the prompt to stop:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan warmup
while :; do
    f="receipt\-$(date +%Y%m%d\-%H%M%S).png"
    appscan scan \-\-mode Gray \-r 200 "$f" || break
    printf \(aqPlace the next sheet, then Enter (q to quit): \(aq
    read \-r answer || break
    [ "$answer" = q ] && break
done
.EE
.RE
.PP
Recover when the Epson stops answering:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan reset
appscan warmup
appscan scan retry.png
.EE
.RE
.PP
Install the firmware (needed once, before the first scan with an Epson
2480/2580):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan firmware
.EE
.RE
.PP
Install the desktop entry, icon and manual page after copying the binary by
hand, and remove them again:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan setup
appscan setup \-\-remove
.EE
.RE
.PP
Collect backend debug output for a scan that fails
.RB ( appscan
reports the messages of
.BR scanimage (1),
debug lines included, only when the scan fails):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
SANE_DEBUG_SNAPSCAN=30 appscan scan test.png 2> snapscan.log
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I \(ti/.local/bin/appscan
The program, as installed by
.IR install.sh .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/appscan/
Data directory; defaults to
.IR \(ti/.local/share/appscan/ .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/appscan/esfw41.bin
The Epson 2480/2580 firmware, installed by
.BR "appscan firmware" .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/appscan/sane.d/
Private SANE configuration for scanners with a quirk profile
.RI ( dll.conf
listing only the profile's backend, the backend's configuration such as
.IR snapscan.conf ,
and an empty
.I dll.d/
directory), written again whenever
.B appscan
needs the scanner.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/applications/io.github.matteospanio.appscan.desktop
Desktop menu entry, installed by
.BR "appscan setup" .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/appscan.svg
Application icon, installed by
.BR "appscan setup" .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/man/man1/appscan.1
This manual page, installed by
.BR "appscan setup" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for data files; ignored unless it is an absolute path.
Default:
.IR \(ti/.local/share .
.B appscan
cannot use a scanner with a quirk profile if its data directory contains a
.B :
or a
.BR \(dq .
.TP
.BI SANE_DEBUG_ BACKEND
Passed on to
.BR scanimage (1)
to enable debug output from a SANE backend, for example
.B SANE_DEBUG_SNAPSCAN=30
for the Epson scanners.
.TP
.B SANE_CONFIG_DIR
For a scanner with a quirk profile,
.B appscan
sets it when it runs
.BR scanimage (1),
replacing any value already set: it points at the private configuration,
with
.I /etc/sane.d
as the fallback.
Other scanners use the SANE configuration of the system.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including a multi\-page scan stopped early that saved at least one
page.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred, such as a scanner that does not answer, missing firmware, or a failing page in a multi\-page scan (the pages before it
are still saved); or the scan was cancelled with
.BR Ctrl\-C .
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage, such as an unknown option, an unsupported output file type,
a value that is not one of the scanner's choices or out of its range, a depth
of 16 with a
.B .jpg
output,
.B \-\-pages
without a
.B .pdf
output, or an output folder that is not writable.
.SH INSTALLATION
.B appscan
is a single binary.
To install the latest release into
.IR \(ti/.local/bin ,
together with the desktop entry, icon and this manual page, and to download
the Epson firmware:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
curl \-fsSL \e
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/matteospanio/appscan/main/install.sh \e
| bash
.EE
.RE
.PP
The script downloads the prebuilt binary for the machine's architecture
(x86_64 or aarch64) from GitHub Releases, or builds it with
.BR cargo (1)
when that is not possible, then runs
.B appscan setup
and
.BR "appscan firmware" .
Missing runtime packages
.RB ( sane\-utils ,
.BR curl ,
.BR p7zip\-full ,
.BR cabextract ,
.BR libgtk\-4\-1 ,
.BR libadwaita\-1\-0 )
are installed with
.B sudo apt\-get
when available.
The prebuilt binary needs glibc 2.35, GTK 4.6 and libadwaita 1.1 or newer.
Set
.B APPSCAN_VERSION
to install a specific release instead of the latest.
Set
.B \%APPSCAN_SKIP_FIRMWARE=1
to skip the firmware download; if it is skipped or fails, run
.B appscan firmware
later.
.PP
To uninstall it, together with the data directory and the firmware:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
curl \-fsSL \e
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/matteospanio/appscan/main/install.sh \e
| bash \-s \-\- \-\-uninstall
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
The first open of an Epson 2480/2580 after power\-on uploads the firmware.
With sane\-backends 1.1.1 this open often fails once;
.B appscan
retries automatically.
.PP
After power\-on or a USB reset the lamp of the Epson needs about 30\(en40
seconds to warm up, while later scans start within a few seconds.
Run
.B appscan warmup
ahead of time to avoid the wait.
.PP
If a scanner with a quirk profile is plugged in but not answering,
.B appscan
resets it automatically before giving up.
.PP
Listing scanners without a profile goes through the system SANE
configuration and can take a while when network backends are enabled;
.B appscan
waits up to 60 seconds.
.PP
Brightness and contrast range from \-100 to 100 at most in the GUI, which can
be narrower than the command line accepts.
.SH BUGS
On the Epson 2480/2580, cancelling before image data flows (during the
firmware upload or warm\-up), or a cancel that hangs in the backend for more
than 10 seconds (which happens about one time in three), makes
.B appscan
kill
.BR scanimage (1)
and reset the scanner.
.PP
SANE reports the film unit of the 2580 as unsupported.
.PP
Closing the GUI while it is still looking for scanners waits until the search
ends, up to 60 seconds, with the window already hidden.
